#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install snap on openSUSE by adding the snappy repository, "
"importing its key, enabling services, and fixing refresh issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:8
msgid "Install snap on openSUSE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:10
msgid ""
"Snap can be installed from the command line on [openSUSE Tumbleweed](https://"
"get.opensuse.org/tumbleweed/) and [openSUSE Leap 15.x](https://"
"get.opensuse.org/leap/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:13
msgid "Older openSUSE releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:15
msgid ""
"The snap daemon, snapd, is only built for currently supported openSUSE "
"releases. See [Support lifetime](https://en.opensuse.org/Lifetime) for "
"details about which releases are currently within the support timeframe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:19
msgid "Add the repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:21
msgid ""
"You need first add the *snappy* repository from the terminal. Tumbleweed "
"users, for example, can do this with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:23
msgid ""
"sudo zypper addrepo --refresh \\\n"
"  https://download.opensuse.org/repositories/system:/snappy/"
"openSUSE_Tumbleweed \\\n"
"  snappy\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:29
msgid ""
"Swap out `openSUSE_Tumbleweed` for your chosen openSUSE distribution, such "
"as `openSUSE_Leap_15.6`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:31
msgid "With the repository added, import its GPG key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:33
msgid "sudo zypper --gpg-auto-import-keys refresh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:37
msgid ""
"Finally, upgrade the package cache to include the new *snappy* repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:39
msgid "sudo zypper dup --from snappy\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:43
msgid "Install snapd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:45
msgid "Snap can now be installed with the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:47
msgid "sudo zypper install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:51
msgid ""
"You then need to either reboot, logout/login or `source /etc/profile` to "
"have /snap/bin added to PATH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:53
msgid "Now enable and start the *snapd* service with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:55
msgid "sudo systemctl enable --now snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:59
msgid "Run the following to enable and start the _snapd.apparmor_ service:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:61
msgid "sudo systemctl enable --now snapd.apparmor\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:65
msgid ""
"At this point, we recommend restarting your machine. You now have *snapd* "
"installed and ready to go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:67
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:69
msgid ""
"If you don’t see the *snapd* update on your system, make sure the repository "
"is refreshing correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:71
msgid ""
"If it's not, remove and re-add the repository with the following two "
"commands (`--refresh` is important), replacing *openSUSE_Tumbleweed* with "
"your specific version of openSUSE:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/opensuse.md:73
msgid ""
"sudo zypper removerepo snappy\n"
"sudo zypper addrepo --refresh \\\n"
"    https://download.opensuse.org/repositories/system:/snappy/"
"openSUSE_Tumbleweed \\\n"
"    snappy\n"
msgstr ""
